   "text": "Skip to main content\nOfficial State of Iowa Website\nAgencies A-Z\nPrograms & Services\nDepartment of Natural Resources\nMain navigation\nPrograms & Services\nPrograms & Services sub-navigation\nPlaces to Go\nPlaces to Go sub-navigation\nThings to Do\nThings to Do sub-navigation\nEnvironmental Protection\nEnvironmental Protection sub-navigation\nAbout\nAbout sub-navigation\nNewsroom\nNewsroom sub-navigation\n404 - Did you wander off trail? We couldn't find the content you're looking for.\nHello there, wayward internet traveler! Let us help you get back on the right trail.\nPrograms & Services\nSearching more by topic? This is a good round-up of the many programs and services we offer to help Iowans join us in caring for our natural resources, such as information on aquatic invasive species, beach monitoring, forestry, lake restoration, reducing food waste and more.\nPlaces to Go\nIf you're looking to get outdoors, we have just the place for you! Here you'll find information about Iowa's state forests, state parks, state preserves, shooting ranges, OHV parks and riding areas, water trails, wildlife management areas and more places to explore.\nThings to Do\nThere's so much to do in Iowa's outdoors! Get out and watch the birds, hit the lake for some boating or kayaking, go camping, fishing, hunting, swimming, snowmobiling and a whole lot more.\nEnvironmental Protection\nTaking care of Iowa's air quality, land quality, water quality is an important part of our agency mission. Here, you'll find info on what you can do in your home and community to care for our natural resources, as well as information for regulated communities.\nAbout the Iowa Department of Natural Resources\nLearn about who does what where in our agency with important points of contact across our agency.\nStill not sure which way to go or need a seasoned trail guide?\nIowa Directory Services offers access to the State of Iowa Employee Directory as well as the option to find a State agency or department.\nIowa DNR staff and office information by county\n(529.4 KB)\n.pdf\nis a detailed county listing of conservation officers and supervisors, recreational safety officers, fisheries and wildlife biologists, environmental field offices, nuisance wildlife control operators, wildlife rehabilitation operators, county recorders and county conservation boards.\nDNR Staff & Offices provides an overview of our various bureaus and divisions and includes staff contact information.\nIowa DNR Customer Service: 515-725-8200\nMonday through Friday, 8 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. CST\n(except for state holidays)\nSecondary Navigation Menu\nHome\n(parent section)\nPrograms & Services\nPrograms & Services submenu\nPlaces to Go\nPlaces to Go submenu\nThings to Do\nThings to Do submenu\nEnvironmental Protection\nEnvironmental Protection submenu\nAbout\nAbout submenu\nNewsroom\nNewsroom submenu\nDepartment of Natural Resources\nFooter Social Media Menu\nIowa DNR Customer Service\n6200 Park Avenue\nSuite 200\nDes Moines, IA 50321\nPhone\n515-725-8200\nHow can we help?\nShare feedback with us\nFooter Menu\nFooter\nContact DNR\nNewsroom\nAccessibility Assistance\nArchived Documents\nContact Menu\nSend Feedback\n© 2026 State of Iowa - Read our accessibility, data, privacy, and other policies.\nGive Feedback",
